# Demonstration of Booleans as first-class world concepts in ForWhile
# This example simulates a LightSwitch creature with an 'on' boolean trait.
# It showcases the toggle pattern and a whenever event rule reactively announcing changes.

creature LightSwitch
  traits
    room is a word
    on is true or false
  end traits

  when born with (room)
    give self the trait room to room
    give self the trait on to no
  end born

  action toggle
    when on is yes
      give on to no
    otherwise
      give on to yes
    end when
  end action
end creature

# Set up event handling to announce when the light is toggled
whenever switch gets trait on changed
  when switch on is yes
    announce switch room + " light is now TURNED ON!"
  otherwise
    announce switch room + " light is now turned off."
  end when
end whenever

# Bring the switch to life
bring switch to life as LightSwitch with ("Living Room")

announce "--- Toggling the switch first time ---"
switch does toggle

announce "--- Toggling the switch second time ---"
switch does toggle
